<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Background</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Chain of Attack Foundation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Chain of Attack (CoA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> provides the foundation for our work, representing a multi-turn attack strategy that leverages semantic relevance between target objectives and model responses. Unlike approaches relying on fixed adversarial prompts, CoA dynamically adapts its attack path based on target model responses.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">CoA measures semantic correlation between model responses and target objectives using SIMCSE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. For target objective <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> and model response <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at turn <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, semantic correlation is computed as <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(t)=\mathrm{SEM}(O,r_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>SEM</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(t)=\mathrm{SEM}(O,r_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SEM}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>SEM</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SEM}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes cosine similarity between embedding vectors. Three correlation scores are measured:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(t)</annotation></semantics></math>: correlation with context,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>: correlation without context, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math>: previous turn correlation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Based on these scores, CoA employs four walking strategies: Next Walk (positive progression), Regen Walk (alternative prompt generation), Back Walk (backtracking), and End Walk (termination). These components interact to create dynamic attack methodology that transforms benign conversations into sequences leading to harmful content generation. Despite its effectiveness, CoA lacks structured exploration of specific conversation patterns, which PE-CoA addresses.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Detailed CoA Walking Strategies</h3>

<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.08859v1/figures/CoA_overview.jpg" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/238;" width="471" height="238" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Structure of CoA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The original Chain of Attack employs four distinct walking strategies based on semantic correlation metrics. Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.2 Detailed CoA Walking Strategies ‣ Appendix A Background ‣ Pattern Enhanced Multi-Turn Jailbreaking: Exploiting Structural Vulnerabilities in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> illustrates how these components interact to create the dynamic attack methodology.
<span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Next Walk</span>: If semantic correlation shows positive progression <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(t)&gt;S(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(t)&gt;S(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the attack proceeds to the next turn. This strategy is used when current interaction appears to move toward the objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regen Walk</span>: If current prompt fails to increase correlation but shows potential (<math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(t)&lt;S(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(t)&lt;S(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}(t)&gt;S(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}(t)&gt;S(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math>), the attack remains at current turn but regenerates alternative prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Back Walk</span>: If neither current prompt nor its alternative without context improves correlation (<math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(t)&lt;S(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(t)&lt;S(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}(t)&lt;S(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}(t)&lt;S(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math>), the attack steps back to previous turns to explore different conversation paths.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">End Walk</span>: The attack terminates upon successfully eliciting harmful responses or reaching predefined maximum turns, ensuring bounded execution.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Pattern Discovery</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Foundations for Pattern Selection</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PE-CoA’s five conversation patterns emerged from established conversation analysis research, identifying structures that might expose LLM training biases. Conversation analysis theory shows that dialogues follow predictable structural patterns through turn-taking systems and sequence organization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sacks (1992)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schegloff (2007)</a></cite>. Speech act theory explains how utterances function as actions within conversations, particularly for requests and information seeking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin (1962)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Searle (1975)</a></cite>. Discourse analysis provided insights into topic coherence and development within structured patterns <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brown and Yule (1983)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Van Dijk (1985)</a></cite>, while social engineering research offered empirical evidence for manipulation patterns adaptable to LLM vulnerability analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hadnagy (2010)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cialdini (2006)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Manual Pattern Analysis and Identification</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Through manual examination of successful multi-turn attacks, five recurring approaches demonstrated effectiveness across scenarios. Educational discussions progress from general concepts to specific applications, following pedagogical structures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Merrill (2002)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Clark (1996)</a></cite>. Personal narratives advance from shared experiences to targeted requests through emotional connection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bruner (1991)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Herman (2003)</a></cite>. Hypothetical scenarios establish fictional frameworks before introducing problematic elements, using cognitive distance to reduce resistance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kahneman and Tversky (1982)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Byrne (2005)</a></cite>. These communication pathways establish trust and context while gradually shifting semantic boundaries.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Pattern Formalization and Vulnerability Targeting</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formalized five patterns targeting specific LLM training aspects:</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Technical-Educational Pattern</span>: Frames attacks as learning processes, exploiting models’ educational helpfulness training while gradually introducing harmful elements in academic contexts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Personal Experience Pattern</span>: Uses personal narrative frameworks to bypass safety mechanisms through empathy and emotional resonance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hypothetical Scenario Pattern</span>: Creates imaginary frameworks distancing requests from direct implementation, exploiting models’ ability to engage with fictional scenarios.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Information Seeking Pattern</span>: Presents attacks as neutral information gathering, exploiting models’ tendencies toward factual and comprehensive responses.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem-Solving Pattern</span>: Frames attacks as practical challenges, exploiting goal-oriented reasoning processes while bypassing safety filters detecting direct harmful instructions.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each pattern was designed to target regions of the vulnerability space <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{gap}</annotation></semantics></math>, representing conversational structures present in pretraining data but not adequately covered by safety training datasets.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Complete PE-CoA Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The complete PE-CoA algorithm integrates the components described in Section 4 into a unified framework that systematically evaluates all conversation patterns against target objectives:</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> PE-CoA: Pattern Enhanced Chain of Attack</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Target objective <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, target model <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{tgt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>tgt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{tgt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, attack model <math id="algx1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{atk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>atk</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{atk}}</annotation></semantics></math>, judge model <math id="algx1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{judge}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>judge</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{judge}}</annotation></semantics></math>, pattern set <math id="algx1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum turns <math id="algx1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, maximum iterations <math id="algx1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, pattern adherence weight <math id="algx1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Attack results for all patterns: <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*},\text{success}_{p}):p\in\mathcal{P}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*},\text{success}_{p}):p\in\mathcal{P}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          Initialize results dictionary <math id="algx1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Results}\leftarrow\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Results</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Results}\leftarrow\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each pattern <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="algx1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Systematic evaluation of all patterns
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            Initialize <math id="algx1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{success}_{p}\leftarrow\text{False}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext>False</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{success}_{p}\leftarrow\text{False}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algx1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{iteration}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>iteration</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{iteration}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algx1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> not <math id="algx1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{success}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{success}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algx1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{iteration}&lt;i_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>iteration</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{iteration}&lt;i_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Pattern-Enhanced Chain Initialization</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Generate candidate sequences <math id="algx1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\text{candidates}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>candidates</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\text{candidates}}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="algx1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\text{atk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>atk</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\text{atk}}</annotation></semantics></math> following pattern <math id="algx1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>’s stages

</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each candidate <math id="algx1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{cand}}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{candidates}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>cand</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mtext>candidates</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{cand}}\in\mathcal{C}_{\text{candidates}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
               Compute score: semantic progression + pattern coherence

</div>
<div id="algx1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             Select highest-scoring sequence <math id="algx1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\leftarrow\arg\max_{\mathcal{T}_{\text{cand}}}\text{score}(\mathcal{T}_{\text{cand}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>cand</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mtext>cand</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\leftarrow\arg\max_{\mathcal{T}_{\text{cand}}}\text{score}(\mathcal{T}_{\text{cand}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Contextual Chain Execution</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             Initialize conversation history <math id="algx1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{0}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{0}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             Initialize current stage <math id="algx1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}(1)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}(1)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> first stage of pattern <math id="algx1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algx1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
               <span id="algx1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Evaluation</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
               Submit prompt <math id="algx1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to target model: <math id="algx1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}_{\text{tgt}}(u_{t}\mid\mathcal{H}_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>tgt</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}_{\text{tgt}}(u_{t}\mid\mathcal{H}_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
               Update history: <math id="algx1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}\leftarrow\mathcal{H}_{t-1}\cup\{(u_{t},r_{t})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}\leftarrow\mathcal{H}_{t-1}\cup\{(u_{t},r_{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
               Compute semantic correlation: <math id="algx1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})\leftarrow\text{SEM}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>SEM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})\leftarrow\text{SEM}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
               Compute pattern adherence: <math id="algx1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(u_{t},p,s_{j}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(u_{t},p,s_{j}(t))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
               Compute combined evaluation: <math id="algx1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathcal{O},r_{t},u_{t},p)\leftarrow\lambda\cdot\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})+(1-\lambda)\cdot\mathcal{A}(u_{t},p,s_{j}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathcal{O},r_{t},u_{t},p)\leftarrow\lambda\cdot\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})+(1-\lambda)\cdot\mathcal{A}(u_{t},p,s_{j}(t))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
            
            
               Evaluate success: <math id="algx1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{success}_{p}\leftarrow J(r_{t},\mathcal{O})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{success}_{p}\leftarrow J(r_{t},\mathcal{O})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
            
            
               <span id="algx1.l24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="algx1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{success}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{success}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
            
            
                <math id="algx1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*}\leftarrow\{u_{1},u_{2},\ldots,u_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*}\leftarrow\{u_{1},u_{2},\ldots,u_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">break</span> <span id="algx1.l26.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Attack successful for this pattern
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
            
            
               <span id="algx1.l27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
            
            
               <span id="algx1.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="algx1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;|\mathcal{T}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;|\mathcal{T}|</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Chain Updating Strategy</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
            
            
                Compute semantic change: <math id="algx1.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{E}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})-\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{E}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t})-\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{O},r_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
            
            
                Decision Engine selects action based on <math id="algx1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algx1.l31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}(u_{t},p,s_{j}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}(u_{t},p,s_{j}(t))</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="algx1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">32:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> positive progression <span id="algx1.l32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">33:</span>
            
            
                  Next Walk: advance to next turn, update stage <math id="algx1.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">34:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="algx1.l34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> high pattern adherence, low semantic progress <span id="algx1.l34.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">35:</span>
            
            
                  Regen Walk: generate alternative prompts for current turn

</div>
<div id="algx1.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">36:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="algx1.l36.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> declining metrics <span id="algx1.l36.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">37:</span>
            
            
                  Back Walk: return to previous turn

</div>
<div id="algx1.l38" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">38:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l38.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l39" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">39:</span>
            
            
                  Pattern Switch: break and try next pattern

</div>
<div id="algx1.l40" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">40:</span>
            
            
                <span id="algx1.l40.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l41" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">41:</span>
            
            
               <span id="algx1.l41.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l41.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l42" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">42:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l42.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l42.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l43" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">43:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l43.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 5: Iterative Chain Refinement</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l44" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">44:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l44.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> not <math id="algx1.l44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{success}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{success}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l44.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l45" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">45:</span>
            
            
               Regenerate attack chain using pattern <math id="algx1.l45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with updated strategy

</div>
<div id="algx1.l46" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">46:</span>
            
            
               <math id="algx1.l46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{iteration}\leftarrow\text{iteration}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>iteration</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>iteration</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{iteration}\leftarrow\text{iteration}+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l47" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">47:</span>
            
            
             <span id="algx1.l47.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l47.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l48" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">48:</span>
            
            
            <span id="algx1.l48.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l48.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l49" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">49:</span>
            
            
            Store results: <math id="algx1.l49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Results}[p]\leftarrow(\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*},\text{success}_{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Results</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>success</mtext><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Results}[p]\leftarrow(\mathcal{T}_{p}^{*},\text{success}_{p})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l50" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">50:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l50.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="algx1.l50.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l51" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">51:</span>
            
            
          <span id="algx1.l51.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <span id="algx1.l51.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Results</span> <span id="algx1.l51.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Comprehensive vulnerability analysis across all patterns
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm Notes:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm systematically evaluates all patterns <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> rather than selecting a single optimal pattern, reflecting the experimental approach described in Section 4.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each pattern evaluation follows the five-step process: initialization, execution, evaluation, updating, and refinement.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The dual evaluation function <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathcal{O},r_{t},u_{t},p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathcal{P}}(\mathcal{O},r_{t},u_{t},p)</annotation></semantics></math> combines semantic correlation with pattern adherence as formalized in Section 4.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stage progression <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is tracked and updated based on pattern-specific transition rules maintained by the Pattern Manager.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm returns comprehensive results enabling vulnerability analysis across all pattern-task combinations, supporting the empirical measurement of <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{M}_{\text{tgt}},p,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mtext>tgt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{M}_{\text{tgt}},p,c)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Vulnerability Analysis Results</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ D.1 Vulnerability Analysis Results ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results ‣ Pattern Enhanced Multi-Turn Jailbreaking: Exploiting Structural Vulnerabilities in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> through <a href="#A4.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ D.1 Vulnerability Analysis Results ‣ Appendix D Detailed Results ‣ Pattern Enhanced Multi-Turn Jailbreaking: Exploiting Structural Vulnerabilities in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> present model-specific vulnerability profiles derived from PE-CoA evaluations. These analyses document two critical dimensions: individual pattern success rates and harm category susceptibility. The results reveal how conversational patterns interact with harm categories across architectures, exposing weaknesses that content-based safety mechanisms frequently overlook.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">For defense development, these results support tailored protective strategies. Models display distinct vulnerability profiles. This specificity helps developers prioritize defenses for their architecture’s most exposed attack vectors.

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Scientifically, the combinatorial space of 10 harm categories and 5 patterns generates 50 distinct attack vectors. Protection against one pattern rarely extends to others, challenging assumptions about generalized robustness. These empirically documented profiles provide foundational evidence for developing context-aware safety alignment that addresses conversational risks while preserving beneficial model capabilities.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">

